{#- The user message of every structured decision (`grimoire.inference.structured_messages`).
    Vars:
      items   — [decisions.Item]: each its `context` (text) and its ordered
                `questions`. A question is a Predicate (`id`, `instructions`),
                a Choice (also `options`, each `id` and `description`, and
                `allow_none`) or a Score (also `levels`, ordered descriptions).
                Option `aliases` are the parser's and are never shown. An
                option's id is quoted, so where it ends is plain whatever it
                holds: a folded id carries a colon of its own
                (`existing:<id>`), and a description may hold another.
      explain — str: the rationale instruction ("" when none is asked for). -#}
{%- for item in items %}
{%- if not loop.first %}

{% endif -%}
Item {{ loop.index0 }}

{{ item.context }}

Questions:
{%- for q in item.questions %}
{%- if q.options is defined %}
- {{ q.id }} (choice{% if q.allow_none %}, or null for none of these{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.options %}
  - "{{ opt.id }}": {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.levels is defined %}
- {{ q.id }} (scale): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for level in q.levels %}
  - {{ loop.index0 }}: {{ level }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
- {{ q.id }} (yes/no): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if explain %}

Rationale, for each item: {{ explain }}
{%- endif %}
